WHAT CHANGED
- B1 AGENTS.md "Run supervisor" bullet: reverted the false clause
  "; run directories are pruned after 7 days (30 for nudged, failed, or deadline runs)".
  Retention only walks identityPaths.recall runs. Intro line and rows 28/30 already
  state the memorian policy correctly.
- B2 planner.ts: tool singles prefer path-derived terms. A term is path-derived when
  it appears in any tool text matching /\/|\.[a-z0-9]{1,6}$/i. Path-derived ranks
  before non-path; newest-first / rarity / length / sequence stay as secondary keys
  (stable sort after rankedTerms). COMMAND_STOPWORDS + user-single exclusion unchanged.
- N1 writeMemorianRunOutcome: mkdir(runDir, { recursive: true, mode: 0o700 }) before
  writing outcome.json so a setup-phase deadline still records the outcome.
- N2 memorian-runner launchOnce: after the judge recorded completed, a post-judge
  dropped/cancelled or dropped/compaction overwrites outcome.json via
  writeMemorianRunOutcome with { status: "dropped", cause, nudged: [] }.
- N3 prune newestFileMtime: empty run dirs fall back to the directory's own mtime;
  non-empty dirs still use newest inner file (running-judge guard).

TDD: tests written first, RED captured (tests only), then implementation, GREEN captured.
